This repository contains my final project for Capstone: Applying Project Management in the Real World, the course that completes the Google Project Management Certificate. The project brings together the knowledge from all previous courses and shows how it applies to a realistic scenario, from initial idea to project closure.

What the project covers:

Initiation: defining goals (SMART, OKRs), project scope, key stakeholders, and stakeholder analysis
Planning: building the project plan, schedule, budget, risk assessment, and RACI matrix
Execution: tracking progress, managing the team, communication, and quality control
Agile and Scrum: applying agile approaches, sprints, and iterative improvement
Closing: evaluating results, documenting lessons learned, and finalizing project documentation

Repository contents: project documents (project charter, plan, risk register, RACI matrix, status reports) and supporting materials.

Goal: to demonstrate the ability to lead a project through its entire life cycle using the tools and frameworks applied in professional practice.
